design.sql_needed:
Yes. One small file, safe to run twice; it adds 3 nullable columns and changes no data.

KAUTION-K1B.sql:
- alter table public.kaution add column if not exists kept jsonb;
- alter table public.rnt_kaution add column if not exists kept jsonb;
- alter table public.ctrl_income_months add column if not exists kau_part jsonb;
- notify pgrst, 'reload schema';
- plus a one-row check.

Why it cannot be avoided:
- The card must remember the month, the amounts and the picked receipt (with its earlier Who pays) to show them again and to change or undo them. No existing column can hold this. deduction_reason is the owner's text and nk_keep belongs to D39.
- kau_part on the month row makes the rent booking exactly-once and reversible in ONE atomic upsert. Without it, the Controlling write and the Kaution write are two separate requests, and a failure between them would double the rent on the next Save.
- A no-SQL version could only book once and could never be edited or undone safely.

Fail-soft: until the file has run, ccKauProbe hides the new rows and the card works exactly as K1.
